From f18a76c39998f0e225f44b532ef486ef70a8d795 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:30:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix compact status tile sizing and battery SOC-range window
 honesty
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CompactStatusCard used aspect-square, which on the row's wide
sm:grid-cols-4 columns produced tall tiles with a lot of empty space —
the opposite of compact. Height now follows the actual content (header
row, one value, one status line).

The battery SOC-range diagnostic always reported the fixed target
window (72h/"3 dygn") regardless of how much history the in-memory
sample buffer actually held. That buffer empties on every add-on
restart and only grows back out over the following days, so right
after a restart the card was claiming a 3-day range while really
showing barely an hour of data. windowHours is now the buffer's actual
current span, with targetWindowHours reported separately so the UI can
show a "still filling up" note instead of a false multi-day claim.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01D9yfcLt9RHbqoZD18y9PT7
